        headers['Retry-After'] = '30';
    }

    return { status, headers };
}
```

The old code emitted `RateLimit` on the exhausted path and lowercase `rate-limit` on the normal path, and never emitted `Retry-After`. Now `X-Rate-Limit` is always present with the exact casing, and `Retry-After: '30'` is added only when the quota is exhausted — no malformed header names remain.

